  "result": "Perfect! All 354 tests pass. I've successfully refactored the invoicing system to separate calculations into a dedicated module:\n\n**New src/totals.js** contains:\n- `lineTotal(line)` - calculates qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n- `lineDiscount(line)` - calculates discount amount on a line\n- `lineVat(line)` - calculates VAT on the line amount after discount\n- `invoiceTotals(invoice)` - calculates { subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js**:\n- Imports these functions from totals.js\n- Re-exports them so existing code is unaffected\n- All other invoice functions remain in invoices.js unchanged\n\n**Backward compatibility maintained**:\n- Every file that imports these functions from invoices.js continues to work unchanged (export.js, render.js, payments.js, statements.js, credits.js, reports.js)\n- No changes needed to any existing tests\n\n**New test/totals.test.js** has 25 comprehensive tests covering:\n- lineTotal with various inputs (single items, zero prices, multiplication)\n- lineDiscount calculations (percentages, defaults, 100% discount, rounding)\n- lineVat calculations (different VAT rates, impact of discounts, VAT-exempt items)\n- invoiceTotals behavior:\n  - Single and multiple lines\n  - Mixed VAT rates\n  - Line discounts\n  - Vouchers\n  - Total clamping at zero\n  - Edge cases (no lines, only VAT-exempt items)\n  - Integer cent preservation throughout calculations\n\nAll 354 tests pass (329 existing + 25 new totals tests).",
